constructed
route: POST /escalations/<id>
status: 200
tack-sends: yes
optional-keys: optionId
built-from: escalation-consult (docket's own recorded view) with state resolved and a resolution block of the keys escalation-accepted.json captured (optionId, content, by, channel, at, appliedAt), and affordances.options empty as the spec says for a resolved view
source: specs/api/operator-api.spec.md "Escalations" (POST /escalations/<id>: optionId and content, answers 200 with the resolved view) and tests/fixtures/operator-v2/escalation-consult.json at 9954b4f8
request: {"optionId":"redis","content":{"note":"the cluster is already deployed"},"actor":"tack"}
docket: docket 0.2.0b6 (API 6), source checkout 9954b4f8, read and not run
date: 2026-10-26
note: an answer to a consult that names an option and carries content; not captured, because docket sends it only while a model runs or a person answers one; every key is one docket writes, the values are made up, or come from the capture or the recording it is built from. The request is in this line because Tack sends it and no capture can: only the escalation-accepted capture holds a request file. It is where the fake learns that an answer may carry content, and that optionId may be left out: the spec lets an input be answered in text alone.
